  "limitations": [
    "This compares retained M-CSA proposal-1 drawings, not independently observed elementary steps or physical atom identities.",
    "All source electron-flow endpoints, including both explicit transferred H atoms and the Glu fragment, are preserved. Flow correspondence preserves direction and endpoint kinds; source-file order is not mechanistic chronology.",
    "The covalent projection preserves displayed elements, formal-charge defaults, raw lone-pair/isotope/R-group tokens and alias presence. It does not complete implicit hydrogens, valence, electronic microstates, or proton balance.",
    "Mg coordination bonds are retained as uncompared context. No native-metal identity or coordination/geometry transfer follows; M0219 native Mg/Ca identity remains unresolved.",
    "Glu fragment correspondence is not residue homology, sequence/structure mapping, or a shared physical protein state. Source placeholder carbons and residue numbering remain explicit metadata.",
    "M0106 pyruvate/decarboxylation and the E2-owned lipoyl carrier remain distinct from M0219 sugar transfer. Do not transfer acceptor identity, multienzyme context, carrier accession/site/pose, or the separate inferred enzyme-reset/cyclization steps.",
    "M0219 proposal 2 and its different protein/reaction context are excluded. The 6HA3 E160Q/F6P-ThDP study does not ground either compared proposal.",
    "No adjacent after-state replay, complete catalytic cycle, conserved enzyme function, canonical reaction map, productive geometry, evidence-tier promotion, or project experiment is established.",
    "The query verifies the declared maps and does not enumerate all graph isomorphisms. The two supplied maps differ only in nonreacting diphosphate oxygen locators; their reaction-endpoint assignments are invariant."
  ],
